docs: digest the documentation to under 20% of its size

Read every doc and every long comment, area by area, and rewrite them as one
plain reference. Same system, same premise; no history, no argument, no
padding. Long comments in files become one line or nothing.

Baseline (main a404bf6): 65 markdown docs, ~13,800 lines; ~9,800 lines of
multi-line comments across ~225 files. Measured: 22,013 -> 3,628 lines (16.5%).

- [x] site: running-it, deploying, NODE, REDIRECTS, MANIFEST, known-issues, CONTENT-TODO, REVIEW-NOTES, site/ comments
- [x] programming: programming.md, instruments/, sync and class code
- [x] members: TENANCY, member-sites, MEMBER-SHOWS, HOLDING-A-BUBBLE, DIRECTORY, LIBRARY-AND-WIZARDS
- [x] payments and identity: payments, PAYMENTS-CHECKLIST, identity, RESERVE-DESIGN, worker/
- [x] machines: STATION, machines/README, BAY, RUNNABLES, INTERMEDIATES, profiles, machine code
- [x] kiosk: KIOSK, SCREENS-DIM, kiosk-1, kiosk/, brand/, kiosk-screen
- [x] troves: troves/*
- [x] crews, attendant, advocate, design notes
- [x] one open list (docs/OPEN.md), one index (docs/README.md), every link repointed
- [x] byte-pinned holders untouched: machines/fcpm, troves/recorder/obs.ps1, troves/recorder/bay/obs-portable.ps1, obs-portable-32.2.2.yml
- [x] tests pass
- [ ] Autumn reads it, area by area
- [ ] .pr back to main's before merge
